5
00:00:18.468 --> 00:00:25.071
Consider this worked case: When designing a
search routine, the specification must

6
00:00:25.071 --> 00:00:33.324
explicitly state the input data, the expected
output, and the maximum allowed time or memory

7
00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:33.874
usage.

8
00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:39.265
input size, with a connecting arrow labeled
'Analysis Bridge'.

9
00:00:39.265 --> 00:00:46.674
List the givens before choosing a method,
because an unstated assumption can change the

10
00:00:46.674 --> 00:00:47.203
conclusion.

11
00:00:47.203 --> 00:00:53.078
This establishes the vocabulary and scope
needed for the remaining sections.

12
00:00:53.186 --> 00:01:00.169
Now define Asymptotic Notation Basics
precisely enough that another learner could

13
00:01:00.169 --> 00:01:02.073
